# !! PLACEHOLDER TEAMS !!
# The handles below do NOT exist yet. Before opening this repository to outside
# contributors a maintainer must:
#   1. Create the teams under the @FutureBuildAIinc organisation
#      (Settings -> Teams). Suggested: maintainers, frontend, legal — or
#      collapse them all to `maintainers` if the split is premature.
#   2. Give each team at least *write* access to this repository. GitHub
#      silently ignores CODEOWNERS entries for teams without write access, so a
#      typo or a missing grant looks exactly like "nothing happened".
#   3. Replace every handle here with the real one.
#   4. Enable "Require review from Code Owners" in the branch protection rule
#      for the default branch, alongside the required "CI" status check.
#
# Syntax: last matching pattern wins, so the specific overrides at the bottom
# take precedence over the catch-all at the top.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default owner for everything not matched below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                   @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application code
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/src/                               @FutureBuildAIinc/frontend
/server/                            @FutureBuildAIinc/frontend @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers

# Money. `money.ts` is the integer-cents boundary, `totals.ts` is the single
# definition of every order total the board, the order page, the customer quote
# and the AI all read, and `sim/pricing.ts` is the tier/contract/volume-break
# engine. A wrong answer in any of these is a commercial error on a B2B order,
# not a display bug — they get maintainer eyes regardless of how small the diff
# looks.
/src/core/lib/money.ts              @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/src/core/domain/totals.ts          @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/src/core/sim/pricing.ts            @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/src/core/actions/                  @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/src/core/domain/customer-quote.ts  @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers

# The framework-free boundary. `src/core/` must not import a UI framework;
# a change that weakens `architecture.test.ts` weakens the one architectural
# guarantee this codebase makes.
/src/core/__tests__/                @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers

# The credential surface. The dealer's Anthropic key is written into
# `.gablenow/secrets.json` by `admin-store.ts`, never read back out to a
# client, and forwarded only by `claude-proxy.ts`. Both files are one mistake
# away from leaking it.
/server/admin-store.ts              @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/server/admin-api.ts                @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers
/server/claude-proxy.ts             @FutureBuildAIinc/maintainers

